\f1\b0  The manuscript is exceptionally disciplined regarding its own boundaries. It avoids the common pitfalls of foundational papers by explicitly stating up front that it does not modify standard quantum mechanics, does not magically derive the Born rule from pure geometry, requires an ad-hoc non-covariant postulate to get a novel prediction, and carries an explicit preferred Lorentz frame.
\fs24 \cf0 \

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
\f0\b\fs32 Rigorous Separation of Boundary Conditions:
\f1\b0  The mathematical distinction between the conservative flow of the closed system (\'a72.2) and the dissipative attractor of the open system (\'a72.3) is well-handled. The Madelung reduction elegantly demonstrates that the mass term alone cannot "self-measure" due to the cosine-in-phase/sine-in-amplitude pairing, clearing an essential consistency hurdle.
\fs24 \cf0 \

\f3\fs40 \cf2 \'95	
