\f6\b \cf0 Overall assessment
\f5\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\qr\partightenfactor0

\f6\b \cf0 1/5 \'97 serious reservations
\f5\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The paper has become more candid and narrower, but its advertised concrete measurement mechanism is not established.\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs36 \cf0 Summary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 The manuscript argues that the Dirac mass term gives closed chiral sectors coherent precession rather than phase locking, while coupling to a dissipative bath can create an Adler/Kuramoto-style locking flow. It interprets measurement as a two-stage dissipative process, with a background configuration selecting one basin in a single-world ontology. It now explicitly concedes that it does not derive the Born rule, does not yet provide the nonlocal selection law, and does not obtain its proposed gravitational Bell signature from standard QED.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs36 \cf0 Improvements over the apparent earlier version\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 The revision has made several important corrections.\
First, it now treats the closed-system chiral calculation as a consistency result: unitary evolution has no attractor, rather than as a derivation of the persistence of superposition.\
Second, it correctly confines Bell correlations to the standard entangled quantum state rather than to a local phase-clock model.\
Third, it demotes the linewidth-dependent gravitational Bell claim from a consequence of the framework to a test of an additional, non-covariant coupling.\
Fourth, \'a73.7 candidly recognizes that ordinary electromagnetic detector couplings do not non-demolition-measure the proposed chiral scalar register. This is intellectually valuable, but it also removes the manuscript\'92s main bridge from the chiral mass term to ordinary detector outcomes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs36 \cf0 Major concerns\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Appendix D does not produce a physical bistable measurement attractor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is the decisive issue.\
The appendix gives\uc0\u8232 [\u8232 \\dot x=-\\Omega y,\\qquad\u8232 \\dot y=\\Omega x-2\\gamma y,\\qquad\u8232 \\dot z=-2\\gamma z.\u8232 ]\
The manuscript then defines an azimuthal angle (\\phi=\\operatorname\{atan2\}(y,x)) and obtains\uc0\u8232 [\u8232 \\dot\\phi=\\Omega-\\gamma\\sin 2\\phi.\u8232 ]\
That angular identity is correct where (r=\\sqrt\{x^2+y^2\}\\neq0). But it is not enough to establish an attracting physical phase state. The same equations give\uc0\u8232 [\u8232 \\dot r=-2\\gamma r\\sin^2\\phi.\u8232 ]\
Thus, for nonzero (\\Omega), the proposed locked angular directions generally occur while the Bloch-vector radius decays. The unconditional density matrix tends to the maximally mixed state, not to either of two distinct pointer states. For (\\Omega=0), every state diagonal in (\\sigma_x) is stationary: that is a continuum, not two selected basins.\
The manuscript has converted a decaying Bloch-vector direction into a measurement outcome. That is not valid. An unconditional Lindblad dephasing equation yields decoherence or relaxation; it does not yield a single outcome. A correct treatment would require a stochastic conditional trajectory, an explicit monitored record, and then an account of why one realization\'97not merely a mixed reduced state\'97is ontic.\
This invalidates the claimed concrete derivation of (K_\{\\rm eff\}) as a measurement-locking rate and the claimed \'93Heisenberg cut as a power threshold.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs28 \cf0 2. The revised \'a73.7 severs the chiral mechanism from ordinary measurement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 The manuscript now states that electromagnetic couplings monitor charge/position-type observables rather than the chiral scalar (\\bar\\psi\\psi). That correction is likely the right direction, but it defeats the paper\'92s original mechanism: the bath model used to motivate locking is no longer the coupling available in ordinary detectors.\
The paper must choose one of two routes:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 derive a detector-scale, QED-consistent mechanism showing how charge/position monitoring induces the claimed chiral synchronization; or\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 narrow the thesis: the chiral mass construction is an analogy or internal-clock interpretation, not the physical mechanism of ordinary measurement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 At present it attempts both positions at once.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs28 \cf0 3. \'93Bath present\'94 does not generically imply an Adler/Kuramoto equation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 A generic traced-out bath gives a reduced master equation, not automatically a phase-only Adler flow with a Lyapunov basin. The cited synchronization literature is strongest for driven, self-sustained, dissipative oscillators; that does not establish the same reduction for a generic detector interaction or a Dirac chiral degree of freedom.\
The paper needs a microscopic Hamiltonian, controlled approximations, a derived completely positive reduced dynamics, and a demonstration that the relevant conditional dynamics has nonzero-radius stable states representing detector records.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs28 \cf0 4. The paper still has no outcome-selection theory\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 The manuscript honestly acknowledges that the Born distribution is postulated and that the background-selection dynamics is unspecified. Those are not peripheral omissions. They are the two ingredients required for the claim that MCI supplies one definite outcome in each run.\
A bath can decohere a reduced state. It does not, by itself, select one ontic outcome. Until the paper supplies a state space for the background variable, its evolution law, its coupling to entangled systems, equivariance or typicality conditions, and a no-signaling proof, \'93concrete measurement mechanism\'94 overstates the result.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs28 \cf0 5. The effective-action and self-energy identifications are asserted too strongly\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 The paper\'92s proposed equivalences between (\\operatorname\{Im\}W), (\\operatorname\{Im\}\\Sigma), dissipative capture, and an Adler lock rate are not established as general facts.\
An imaginary part of an in/out effective action, an influence-functional decoherence term, a finite quasiparticle linewidth, and a detector record are distinct constructions. A complex pole can describe decay or loss of coherence; it does not by itself prove phase locking, a pointer state, or outcome selection. These identifications should be presented as heuristic analogies unless derived in one consistent microscopic model.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs28 \cf0 6. The gravitational Bell proposal remains outside the framework\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 The revision correctly derives a common-mode cancellation under standard QED. But the remaining effect requires an undefined extra term that is admitted to be non-covariant and absent from standard QED. A null experiment would constrain a family of such added couplings; it would not falsify MCI as formulated.\
The manuscript should remove \'93clean falsification test\'94 language unless it supplies a gauge-consistent, dimensionally specified, Lorentz-breaking effective theory with a finite parameter set and independent constraints.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs28 \cf0 7. Several broad physical claims require narrowing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 The claim that irreversible openness occurs only at amplitude-deforming boundaries, gradients, or curvature is too broad. Environmental monitoring can arise through scattering, field noise, radiative coupling, and distributed interactions without fitting that taxonomy. Likewise, MRI polarization supplies a useful illustration of a weak biased thermal ensemble, but it does not establish a universal phase-bearing measurement reference.\
The Zitterbewegung discussion should also distinguish a formal positive/negative-energy interference frequency from an empirically established, continuously physical internal clock carried by a positive-energy particle.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f6\b\fs36 \cf0 Required revisions\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f5\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Withdraw the claim that Appendix D derives bistable measurement outcomes or a Heisenberg-cut phase transition.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Replace Appendix D with a conditional quantum-trajectory calculation that includes the measurement record, or label it strictly as an analogy about dephasing.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Resolve the \'a73.7 problem by deriving a real detector coupling from QED, or remove the claim that the chiral mass channel supplies the ordinary measurement mechanism.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Recast (\\operatorname\{Im\}W), (\\operatorname\{Im\}\\Phi), and (\\operatorname\{Im\}\\Sigma) as distinct quantities unless a single explicit model proves their required relation.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Rewrite the abstract, title claims, and conclusion so that MCI is presented as an incomplete interpretive program, not a concrete solution of outcome selection.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Specify the proposed background ontology and dynamics, or state unequivocally that definite outcomes remain postulated.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	7	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Supply reproducible code for Appendix D, pinned dependencies, output figures, and tests that check the full density matrix\'97not only the extracted phase angle.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	8	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Add a quantitative preferred-frame analysis or remove implications that existing Lorentz tests are likely evaded.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	9	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Replace the gravitational-Bell \'93prediction\'94 language with an explicitly parametrized speculative extension.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

